<title>BELGIUM: UM profit slips, sees improvement.</title>
<headline>UM profit slips, sees improvement.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of Belgian francs)</p>
<p>    Group net profit		    281  vs    311</p>
<p>    Consolidated net profit	   285  vs    439</p>
<p>    Taxes				   188  vs    206</p>
<p>    Exceptional loss		    309  vs    469</p>
<p>    Current profit			782  vs  1,114</p>
<p>NOTE - Belgian non-ferrous metals group Union Miniere SA said it expected an improvement in current profit in the second half, barring a significant fall in metals prices. It noted the economic environment had not changed much since June 30.  </p>
<p>    Financial charges		   117  vs    488</p>
<p>    Operating profit		    829  vs  1,493</p>
<p>    Turnover			   64,752  vs 71,517</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
